<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chimalpopoca</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. <a href="/years/1417">1417</a>–<a href="/years/1427">1427</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chimalpopoca was the third ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexica">Mexica</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tenochtitlan">Tenochtitlan</a> in the early fifteenth century, when they were tributaries of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tepanecs">Tepanec</a> city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azcapotzalco">Azcapotzalco</a>. During the succession struggle after the death of the Tepanec ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tezozomoc">Tezozomoc</a> in 1426, he was allegedly murdered on the orders of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maxtla">Maxtla</a>. His successor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/itzcoatl">Itzcoatl</a> formed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aztec-empire">Triple Alliance</a> that founded the Aztec Empire.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chimalpopoca.jpg" alt="Chimalpopoca" width="320" height="246" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tovar, Juan de, circa 1546-circa 1626 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chimalpopoca,_the_Third_Aztec_King_(Reigned_1417%E2%80%9327)_WDL6720.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
